* EDIT DRIVER - THE RECORD LAYOUT AND THE EDIT RULES BOTH ARRIVE AS MACROS
*
* Nothing in this file declares a single field of EDITIN or EDITGOOD, and
* nothing in it tests one.  Parsed WITHOUT the macros, this program has two
* files with no fields, one working-storage counter, and a lineage that is
* empty - and it still looks like a finished answer.  That is what stage 1
* exists to prevent.
*
* %CUSTREC takes the record's starting position as a positional parameter.
* %EDITCHK takes none: it is the edit rules, and it is where WS-ERRORS is
* actually set.
*
FILE EDITIN FB(200 2000)
%CUSTREC 1
*
FILE EDITGOOD FB(200 2000)
%CUSTREC 1
*
DEFINE WS-ERRORS W 2 N 0
*
JOB INPUT EDITIN NAME EDITJOB
  WS-ERRORS = 0
%EDITCHK
  IF WS-ERRORS = 0
     MOVE LIKE EDITIN EDITGOOD
     PUT EDITGOOD
  END-IF
